{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenBaseline","namespace":"app.options.ibkr.gex","doc":"The open-interest baseline identity active for an epoch, under the reserved key __baseline|<tradeDate>|<epoch>. PART OF THE IDENTITY LEDGER: the recovery reader takes the highest epoch it observes as its mint-above basis and restores the contentHash of the highest NON-REVOKED epoch. Note that only this record type advances that basis — a revocation does not — so every spent epoch needs one of these, including a revoked one. Published to options.ibkr.gex.status.v2 by databento-gex-service's pre-open IBKR GEX publisher (IbkrPreOpenService). The predecessor topic options.ibkr.gex.status carried hand-built JSON strings until 2026-10-17; this record reproduces that JSON FIELD FOR FIELD AND NAME FOR NAME. That is a hard requirement, not tidiness: the feed gateway converts these records to JSON for the browser with AvroJson, which emits exactly the published record's own fields, and option-chain.js reads them BY NAME. Renaming or retyping a field here changes what the browser receives. The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME, under RecordNameStrategy. That is deliberate and not the Confluent default, and here it is load-bearing rather than merely conventional: this ONE topic carries nine distinct value shapes, and a topic-name subject could not hold nine schemas. It also keeps one subject across environments, where TopicNameStrategy would mint a different subject per environment because the topic name carries the environment's TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"vendorSession","type":"string","doc":"The vendor session date the baseline was drawn from."},{"name":"contentHash","type":"string","doc":"Hash of the baseline's content, used to decide whether a restored baseline is the same one. The predecessor reader extracted this by SUBSTRING SEARCH over the JSON; with this schema it is read as a typed field."}]}